    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flight times from Tokyo to Osaka are expedited by high-speed bullet trains making the travel duration about 111 minutes. The Shinkansen's journey, however, remains substantially quicker at approximately 228 minutes in total. While in-flight, you can indeed access reliable coverage to keep you connected, though the distances between Tokyo and Osaka, and Osaka and Fukuoka can restrict WiFi accessibility into the plane. On the Shinkansen, you'll find reasonably good WiFi and workspaces available, particularly on the wider Hikari, Kodama, and Nozomi services, catering to your need for productivity en route. Prime-time fares usually come at a steeper rate, but it guarantees not just WiFi connectivity but also a smooth ride, free from the turbulence of airport transfers and no additional waiting at airports. The Shinkansen provides a serene environment, conducive to focus and wellbeing which is valuable for business travelers.",
